prose style and its implications for audience and genre from classical rhetoric to the humanist revival of a 'classical' style. A basic foundation in Latin morphology, syntax, and vocabulary is assumed. Intermediate and advanced topics in post-Classical idioms and syntax will be treated as they arise, with the goal of improving the facility with which students approach, read, and, especially, understand Latin writings from the Middle Ages.\u00a0In addition to studying the practice(s) of style and Latin prose composition, modern approaches to stylistic analysis, and the intersections of style and identity, participants will gain a working knowledge of medieval theories of prose style as articulated in treatises on the\u00a0genera dicendi,\u00a0ars dictaminis,\u00a0and\u00a0ars praedicandi, as well as medieval (and modern) discussions of\u00a0cursus\u00a0and\u00a0clausulae.", "catalogBreadth": "(HB)", "catalogDistr": "(ALC-AS, LA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "Satisfies Option 1.", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2839, "crseId": 372071, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "LATIN", "catalogNbr": "5212", "titleShort": "Elementary Latin II", "titleLong": "Elementary Latin II", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 6624, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "11:20AM", "timeEnd": "12:10PM", "startDt": "01/23/2023", "endDt": "05/09/2023", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 10, "netid": "aha92", "firstName": "Hana", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Aghabab